  - { t: "Gift finder", d: "Three quick questions (who it's for, the occasion, what he uses now) and the site suggests the right product with a note ready to go." }
  - { t: "Gift notes", d: "Shoppers write a card message and see a preview before checkout. The note follows the order through." }
  - { t: "A routine he'll keep", d: "Two steps with live timers on the page: 30 seconds to wash, 15 to moisturise. It shows how little effort it takes." }
  - { t: "Cart and checkout", d: "A slide-out cart, a free-shipping progress bar, and secure checkout on Stripe. The 10% welcome code works on first orders only." }
  - { t: "Accounts and orders", d: "A small backend, ready to switch on, so customers can sign up and see past orders. Prices always come from the database, never from the browser." }
  - { t: "Built for search", d: "Every product and journal post has its own title, description and structured data, with a sitemap ready. Google is kept out until launch day." }
decisions:
  - "Write for the buyer, not the user. Headlines and gift guides talk to the person choosing the present."
  - "Keep the range to three products, so nobody has to work out which one he needs."
  - "Put all the copy in one place, so the owner can change words and prices without touching code."
  - "Hide the site from Google until the real photos, ingredients and reviews are in, so the first version Google sees is the finished one."
